cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Saint Anthony's Channel ReID: Vessel Re-Identification From a Fixed Camera"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24015510"
url: "https://mf1999.github.io/sac-reid-page/"
license: "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fabijanić"
    given-names: "Matej"
    affiliation: "University of Zagreb, Faculty of Electrical Engineering and Computing"
    email: "matej.fabijanic@fer.hr"
abstract: >-
  Image crops of vessels in the Saint Anthony's Channel near Šibenik, Croatia,
  from one fixed camera. 712 identities and 56,615 crops in the Market-1501 layout,
  with train, val and test splits. The test split comes from the hand-annotated
  ground truth of 59 multi-object tracking sequences.
keywords:
  - re-identification
  - vessel re-identification
  - ship re-identification
  - maritime computer vision
  - maritime surveillance
  - object re-identification
  - Market-1501
  - metric learning
  - image retrieval
  - fixed camera
  - multi-object tracking
